          "source_quote": "διαλλάξας πρὸς ἑαυτὸν εὐθύστερον",
          "english_quote": "After quickly reconciling to himself",
          "issue": "εὐθύστερον expresses temporal succession, 'soon afterward,' rather than the speed with which reconciliation was accomplished. 'Quickly' introduces a manner claim and loses the subsequent timing. The note's alternatives 'more readily' and 'more directly' likewise fail to disclose that temporal sense. This is a translation problem, not evidence of corruption in the image-checked reading.",
          "suggested_revision": "Recast the sentence provisionally as: 'Having soon afterward reconciled to himself many who were trying to expose him as a sorcerer, and having sacrificed an ox under the pretext of a banquet and given them a feast, he beset them with various diseases and subjected them to demons.' Replace the lexical note with an explanation of εὐθύστερον as 'soon afterward,' retaining the supplied Greek without emendation. The replacement requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    },
